0549+  D3A5             ;*
0550+  D3A5             ;* Perform a global rotation, i.e. rotate the centers
0551+  D3A5             ;* (16-bit signed value) by the rotation matrix.
0552+  D3A5             ;*
0553+  D3A5             ;* The multiplication multiplies to get a 24-bit result
0554+  D3A5             ;* and then divides the result by 64 (mult by 4).  To
0555+  D3A5             ;* perform the signed multiplication:
0556+  D3A5             ;*   - multiply C*y as normal
0557+  D3A5             ;*   - if y<0 then subtract 256*C
0558+  D3A5             ;*   - if C<0 then subtract 2^16*y
0559+  D3A5             ;*
0560+  D3A5             ;* Parameters: .Y = number of points to rotate
0561+  D3A5             ;*
0562+  D3A5             ;* v2 -- rewritten for efficiency.  Old version computed
0563+  D3A5             ;*              1/64 row1*(cx,cy,cz) + 1/64 row2*(cx,cy,cz) + ...
0564+  D3A5             ;*       New version computes
0565+  D3A5             ;*              [ cx*column1 + cy*column2 + cz*column3 ] / 64
0566+  D3A5             ;* Actually, above seems complicated, and doesn't offer
0567+  D3A5             ;* a huge advantage, so has been skipped for now 3/5/99.
0568+  D3A5             ;*
0569+  D3A5             
0570+  D3A5             ; MULTAY   MAC              ;Multiply A*Y, store in var1, A
