0899+  D54C             ;* ROTPROJ -- Perform local rotation and project points.
0900+  D54C             ;*
0901+  D54C             ;* Setup needs:
0902+  D54C             ;*   Rotation matrix
0903+  D54C             ;*   Pointer to math table (MATMULT = $AF-$B0)
0904+  D54C             ;*   Pointers to point list (P0X-P0Z = $69-$6E)
0905+  D54C             ;*   Pointers to final destinations (PLISTYLO ... = $BD...)
0906+  D54C             ;*     (Same as used by POLYFILL)
0907+  D54C             ;*   Pointers to lists of centers (CXLO CXHI... = $A3-$AE)
0908+  D54C             ;*   .Y = Number of points to rotate (0..N-1)
0909+  D54C             ;*   .X = Object center index (index to center of object)
0910+  D54C             ;*
0911+  D54C             ;* New addition:
0912+  D54C             ;*   C set means rotate and project, but C clear means just
0913+  D54C             ;*   rotate.  If C=0 then need pointers to rotation
0914+  D54C             ;*   destinations ROTPX,ROTPY,ROTPZ=$59-$5E.
0915+  D54C             ;*
0916+  D54C             ;* v2: Now two rotation matrices, local and viewpoint.
0917+  D54C             ;*     Points are rotated by local matrix; if projecting,
0918+  D54C             ;*     points are now rotated by viewpoint matrix, then
0919+  D54C             ;*     projected.
0920+  D54C             ;*
0921+  D54C             ;*     Rotated z-coordinates are now stored in PLISTZLO/HI
0922+  D54C             ;*     ($6F/$71)
0923+  D54C             ;*
0924+  D54C             ;*     If C=0, then coords just stored in PLISTXLO etc.,
0925+  D54C             ;*     as this now seems to be a pretty useless function.
0926+  D54C             ;*     (low bytes only!).
0927+  D54C             ;*
0928+  D54C             
0929+  D54C             
0930+  D54C             ; SMULT   MAC              ;Signed multiplication
0931+  D54C             		; STA MATMULT
0932+  D54C             		; EOR #$FF
